# T0075 — Task Groups refactor (slice 1)

**Task:** T0075 · id `87` · Ready · project 4 (TaskMesh) · Urgent  
**Branch (after approval):** `T0075-task-groups`

**Children (out of scope):** T0077 auto-tag · T0078 nav sub-lists · T0079 Tags/Project filter fields · T0080 Project Phase field

## Goal

Replace list-view **Phases** with **Task Groups**: project-scoped named sections. A group may store a **filter** and **color**. Group filters **override** the list filter for that section. Membership (`tasks.phaseId`) is **not** used for placement.

## Decisions (interview)

| # | Decision |
|---|----------|
| B | **Start empty** — wipe existing phase rows; do not keep names |
| C | **Filter-only** sections; a task may appear under multiple groups. Subtle **Duplicate** indicator on the title when it does |
| D | Drag **into** another group is a **no-op** (no membership write; avoids T0077 rework) |
| E | Keep **Unassigned** for now (may go away later) |
| F | **Project Tasks list only** (All Tasks stays flat) |
| G | Filter fields = T0053: State, Priority, Title, Number |
| H | Persist filter + color on the **group row in Postgres** |
| I | Double-click title opens **modal** (no inline rename) |
| J | Same **16-swatch** palette; color the **full group bar** |

## Scope

**In**

- Rebrand list Phase UI/copy to **Group** (headers, add/delete, drag handle titles)
- Schema + API for groups: `name`, `sortOrder`, `color`, saved `filter` (same JSON shape as `TaskListFilter`)
- Wipe current phases; `tasks.phase_id` null; list ignores `phaseId` for sectioning
- Group edit **modal**: rename, filter builder (reuse T0053 clause UI), color (`ColorPopover`), save/cancel; delete stays confirm
- Filter **icon** to the right of the count when a filter is saved; **tooltip** = existing breadcrumb formatter
- Per-section listing: active group filter **only** (ignore list filter). Empty filter → **no tasks** under that group (bar still shows)
- **Unassigned**: tasks in the project that match the **list** filter and are **not** in any group’s result set
- Duplicate chip/label on the task title when `task.id` is in **two or more group** sections
- Group bar color from saved hex
- Reorder groups (existing drag); reorder tasks **within** a section if that already exists without writing `phaseId`
- Hide/stop using the task modal **Phase** picker this slice (T0080 brings a real Phase field)

**Out**

- Auto-tag (T0077), nav sub-lists (T0078), Tags/Project/Assignee filter fields (T0079), Project Phase field (T0080)
- All Tasks grouped sections
- Unassigned edit modal / color
- Migrating old phase names or membership

## Approach

### Schema (MINOR on finish-up)

1. Drop FK `tasks.phase_id` → `project_phases` (keep nullable `phase_id` column for T0080; null all rows).
2. Rename `project_phases` → `task_groups` (columns: existing `id`, `project_id`, `name`, `sort_order`, timestamps + **`color` text null** + **`filter` jsonb null**).
3. **Delete all `task_groups` rows** (start empty).
4. Drizzle `schema.ts`, generate SQL, update `docs/database/*`, `npm run docs:sync-schema`.

Validate `filter` JSON against the T0053 shape (`clauses` / `joins`, known fields/operators) on write; reject invalid payloads.

### API

Rename project nested routes from phases → groups, e.g. `/api/v1/projects/:projectId/groups` (CRUD, reorder). PATCH accepts `name`, `color`, `filter` (null/empty = no filter). Update clients, import/export (stop treating `phaseId` as list membership; export can still emit empty `phaseId`), assistant tools labels if they say “Phase” for this table.

Keep a short compatibility shim only if something external still hits `/phases` (private app: prefer a clean rename + grep).

### List rendering (`TaskBoard`)

For each group (sort order):

- If `filter` active → `evaluateTaskListFilter(projectTasks, group.filter)` (do **not** AND with list filter)
- Else → `[]`

Unassigned: `evaluateTaskListFilter(projectTasks, listFilter)` minus ids already shown in any group.

Duplicate: if a task id appears in more than one group list, show a small muted **Duplicate** marker on the title (tooltip optional: “Also shown in another group”).

Drop on another group / Unassigned: **no-op** (no PATCH `phaseId`). Do not visually “stick” a move.

### Modal + header

Replace inline rename with `onOpenGroup(id)` → modal. Double-click **title** only (not collapse/count/delete). Unassigned: no modal.

Reuse `TaskListFilterBar` / modal row UI inside the group modal (or extract shared clause editor). Apply writes PATCH to the group.

Filter icon: same visual language as the list filter button; `title={formatFilterBreadcrumb(filter)}`.

### Copy / chrome

“Add phase” → “Add group”; delete confirm talks about the **group**, not unassigning tasks (delete does not change tasks).

